    "failure": "No supported new mechanism opening after inspecting all 12 received records. Counting repeated S/V and M/L schedules or AM/AI wording as new discoveries would misattribute existing constructions. Contrary resource dependencies require intact H for tapping and detached/free S or M for compound retention; existing clip refutes the inference that zero impacts necessitate disassembly. The unresolved tension is extra operator work and H displacement versus component-specific availability with no later-demand or wear model. Supplied schedules include their release primitives; no omitted operation is invented as an actual defect.",
    "invariant": "Retain at least 4 at ticks 3,4,5,6, then separate panels with every installed retainer removed by boundary 10; preserve all available identities without damage, discard, substitution or outside resource, one operator/action per tick with next-boundary completion.",
    "permitted_variable": "Choose only an existing J0-supported construction and preserve its exact preconditions/release order; grammar is soft, b stays 2. No new physical opening is supported. The exchange changes provenance transport and contract clarity, not a mechanism or required function; no unconditional unmeasured-Q promise.",
