  "handoff": {
    "summary": "{\"capsule\":{\"case_sha256_canonical_encoded\":\"912ce6efad9bde5c34d99f398c74493621d8359504b2f7dc437e176113fcd56c\",\"pools\":[{\"candidates\":[{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"P1\",\"op\":\"tap\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"P2\",\"op\":\"tap\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"P1\",\"op\":\"pull\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"P2\",\"op\":\"pull\",\"tick\":8}],\"burden\":\"Four operator ticks and two impacts; H stays assembled. Removal needs two separate pulls. No new component or restoration action.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"One pin alone supplies only 2; either pull before the final required hold boundary would reduce capacity below 4. Tapping with detached H is unsupported.\",\"id\":\"AC20-PRE-implementation-P1\",\"lineage\":\"Initial precursor from task facts J03,J04 and the explicit conventional archive J10; no received proposal or analog source.\",\"mechanism\":\"Intact H installs P1 and P2; their capacities add to 4. Pulls remove their contributions individually.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled proposal: 4 units from boundary 2 until boundary 8, then 2 until boundary 9, then no installed pins. The conventional precursor is not locally original.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J04\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J11\",\"J12\"]},{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"detach\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"V\",\"op\":\"install\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"S,V\",\"op\":\"insert\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"S,V\",\"op\":\"withdraw\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"V\",\"op\":\"remove\",\"tick\":8},{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"assemble\",\"tick\":9}],\"burden\":\"Six operator ticks including optional hammer restoration; zero impacts. H cannot tap while S is deployed. V installation alone provides no stated retention, so all three setup actions must finish by boundary 3.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Leaving H intact denies the required free S. Delayed insertion misses tick 3. Pins or another non-pin assembly cannot supplement the sleeve. Skipping withdrawal prevents the specified release sequence.\",\"id\":\"AC20-PRE-implementation-P2\",\"lineage\":\"Initial construction derived solely from J03 and J06; it has not been revised by assistance. Full precursor schedule preserved.\",\"mechanism\":\"Detach frees S; installed V plus inserted S supplies min(4,4)=4. Withdrawal removes the active stem contribution, removal clears V, and final assembly restores H using free M and S.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled proposal: 4 units beginning boundary 3 through boundary 7; withdrawal completes at 8, V removal at 9, and H restoration at 10. Compared with the two-pin precursor, impacts fall from two to zero while operator actions increase from four to six. Real-world novelty is undetermined.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J06\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J11\",\"J12\"]},{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"detach\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"M\",\"op\":\"place\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"L\",\"op\":\"route\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"L\",\"op\":\"unroute\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"M\",\"op\":\"lift\",\"tick\":8},{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"assemble\",\"tick\":9}],\"burden\":\"Six operator ticks including optional H restoration; zero impacts. M is occupied through boundary 9, keeping H unavailable for tapping. Both setup actions after disassembly and both release actions are necessary.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Placement alone or routing alone does not establish retention. H cannot remain assembled while M is placed. Omitting unroute or lift leaves the prescribed release incomplete.\",\"id\":\"AC20-PRE-implementation-P3\",\"lineage\":\"Initial construction from J03 and J07, independently generated within the implementation concern; no other investigator, proposal, or analog was consulted.\",\"mechanism\":\"Detach frees M; place M then route L supplies min(4,4)=4 through their joint assembly. Unroute ends retention and lift frees M; free M and S allow assembly at tick 9.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled proposal: 4 units from boundary 3 through boundary 7; unroute completes at 8, lift at 9, and H restoration at 10. Relative to the sleeve, the occupied hammer component changes from S to M while action count and modeled capacity match. No measured mechanics or global originality claim.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J07\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J11\",\"J12\"]}],\"handoff_residue\":\"The non-pin setups have no spare setup tick before boundary 3 and displace hammer availability. Added reassembly is a burden choice, not a hard requirement. Equal modeled capacity does not make sleeve and loop resource occupancy interchangeable.\",\"job_id\":\"AC20-PRE-implementation\",\"raw_sha256\":\"7ece3f059b6428dedec4b9f9af29df47f57250487e86e0ce2d357a8c12a18edd\",\"source_limits\":[\"All outcomes are finite-model proposals pending root replay, not measured physics or final self-grades.\",\"J10 names two-pin and clip constructions as conventional; absence of sleeve or loop from that archive cannot prove wider novelty.\",\"Q theta remains unknown in {0,4}. No unconditional Q-only construction is advanced; measurement itself creates no retention.\",\"No changed impact ladder, adhesive, welding, sustained manual support, extra resource, or unlisted operation is used.\"]},{\"candidates\":[{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"C\",\"op\":\"install\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"C\",\"op\":\"remove\",\"tick\":7}],\"burden\":\"Two operator actions and zero taps. H remains intact and its parts remain available. No operator action is needed during ticks 3-6. C is occupied from boundary 3 until boundary 8 and cannot serve another location.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Installation completing after boundary 3 misses required retention; removal completing within the hold window breaks service. Failing to remove C by boundary 10 breaks release.\",\"id\":\"PRE-SVC-C\",\"lineage\":\"Initial precursor independently constructed from the current J0 facts; conventional clip construction explicitly acknowledged by J10.\",\"mechanism\":\"install(C) completes at boundary 3 and supplies 4 units. remove(C) at tick 7 completes at boundary 8, removing the sole retainer and permitting separation.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled: retention is 4 at each required tick; all installed retainers are gone by boundary 8. Upkeep requires no stipulated intervention during holding; post-service C is free and H is intact. Compared with the other two candidates, fewer actions and no H disassembly are required. No wear, inspection interval or reliability claim follows from the axioms; local originality is excluded by J10.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J05\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\"]},{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"detach\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"V\",\"op\":\"install\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"S,V\",\"op\":\"insert\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"S,V\",\"op\":\"withdraw\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"V\",\"op\":\"remove\",\"tick\":8},{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"assemble\",\"tick\":9}],\"burden\":\"Six operator actions including asset restoration; zero taps. S is occupied in V until boundary 8, so H cannot support tapping while disassembled. M remains free. V remains installed until boundary 9. No intervention is required during holding.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Intact H leaves S unavailable for insertion. Omitting withdrawal prevents valid sleeve removal; omitting remove(V) leaves an installed retainer at the deadline. Earlier withdrawal would interrupt the hold window.\",\"id\":\"PRE-SVC-SV\",\"lineage\":\"Initial precursor independently constructed solely from J03 and J06 under the current service contract; no proposal or analog received.\",\"mechanism\":\"detach(H) frees S at boundary 1; V installs at boundary 2; S insertion completes at boundary 3 with min(4,4)=4 retention. Withdrawal completes at boundary 8, removing retention; sleeve removal completes at boundary 9. Assembly restores H at boundary 10.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled: 4 units throughout ticks 3-6; retention ends at boundary 8 and the last installed retainer is removed by boundary 9, permitting separation. Upkeep after release returns S and M to intact H by boundary 10 and leaves V free. Compared with C, this needs four additional actions and temporarily removes hammer availability. Reassembly restores tool configuration without creating retention. Wear, jamming, repeated-cycle endurance and field maintainability remain unknown; archive absence alone does not establish broader novelty.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J06\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\"]},{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"detach\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"M\",\"op\":\"place\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"L\",\"op\":\"route\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"L\",\"op\":\"unroute\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"M\",\"op\":\"lift\",\"tick\":8},{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"assemble\",\"tick\":9}],\"burden\":\"Six operator actions including restoration, zero taps. M is occupied until boundary 9, L until boundary 8; H is unavailable for tapping while detached. S remains free. No manual support or hold-period action is assumed.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Placing M alone gives no stated 4-unit assembly. Routing late misses boundary 3. Unrouting alone does not complete recovery: lift(M) remains required, and assembly cannot precede freeing M.\",\"id\":\"PRE-SVC-ML\",\"lineage\":\"Initial precursor independently constructed solely from J03 and J07 under current J0 facts; no analog bank or other role output exposed.\",\"mechanism\":\"Detach completes at boundary 1, placement at boundary 2 and routing at boundary 3. The conjunction supplies min(4,4)=4. Unrouting completes at boundary 8, then lifting completes at boundary 9; assembly completes at boundary 10.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled: 4 units at ticks 3-6; unrouting ends retention at boundary 8 and lifting clears the remaining installed assembly component at boundary 9, permitting separation. Upkeep restores intact H by boundary 10 and frees L. The action count matches S/V, but the occupied hammer component and release order differ: L must be unrouted before M is lifted. No elastic behavior, inspection rule, fatigue resistance or physical advantage over S/V is established. This is an alternate stipulated mechanism, not demonstrated field novelty.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J07\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\"]}],\"handoff_residue\":\"Clip achieves the required modeled service with two actions; the other candidates use six to restore H. Withdrawal or unrouting ends retention before final component recovery. No stipulated wear model exists. The original invalid service remains invalid; this fresh precursor neither imports its unseen contents nor retroactively repairs its verdict.\",\"job_id\":\"COV-AC20-PRE-service\",\"raw_sha256\":\"dfc13c407de2fd6bb9f79d626cdd04d2700041f05a0134036ac2ad0dfdf09dde\",\"source_limits\":[\"Only literal J01-J12 facts used; no direct input jobs exist, so all input_job_refs are empty.\",\"All candidate outcomes are modeled predictions, not observed execution or self-grading. Root replays action effects.\",\"Service requirement and release deadline are unchanged. No declared ladder cell or impact-budget change is made.\",\"Q theta cannot be assumed; measurement creates no retention. No Q construction is claimed.\",\"Upkeep predictions cover resource recovery and tool reassembly only; no wear or recurring maintenance axiom is available.\",\"No claim about an unseen original schedule is invented; the original invalid service remains invalid.\"]},{\"candidates\":[{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"C\",\"op\":\"install\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"C\",\"op\":\"remove\",\"tick\":7}],\"burden\":\"Two actions, zero impacts; C occupied boundaries3-8; H intact. Fewer actions than either decomposed assembly.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Late installation, premature removal or C left installed at10 breaks the contract.\",\"id\":\"UNION-C\",\"lineage\":\"Received PRE-SVC-C unchanged; AI supplies an accounting annotation only. Conventional under J10.\",\"mechanism\":\"C directly supplies4; removing C ends holding and clears the only retainer.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled: installation completes3, holds4 at3-6, removal completes8. No field efficacy claim.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J05\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\",\"AI\"]},{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"detach\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"V\",\"op\":\"install\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"S,V\",\"op\":\"insert\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"S,V\",\"op\":\"withdraw\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"V\",\"op\":\"remove\",\"tick\":8},{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"assemble\",\"tick\":9}],\"burden\":\"Six actions, zero impacts; H unavailable while S deployed. V alone has no stated retention; no spare setup tick.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Intact H denies S; late insertion misses3; missing V removal prevents full release.\",\"id\":\"UNION-SV\",\"lineage\":\"Received implementation-P2 and PRE-SVC-SV schedules match and stay unchanged. AM/AI annotations add no construction.\",\"mechanism\":\"Detach frees S; V plus S insertion supplies min(4,4)=4. Withdraw S before removing V; then restore H.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled: holds from3, withdrawal completes8, V removal9, restoration10. Four extra actions versus C.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J06\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\",\"AM\",\"AI\"]},{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"detach\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"M\",\"op\":\"place\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"L\",\"op\":\"route\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"L\",\"op\":\"unroute\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"M\",\"op\":\"lift\",\"tick\":8},{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"assemble\",\"tick\":9}],\"burden\":\"Six actions, zero impacts; M occupied until9, L until8. H unavailable; same action count as S/V with different component occupancy.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Late routing misses3; lifting without unrouting or restoring before M is free violates preconditions.\",\"id\":\"UNION-ML\",\"lineage\":\"Received implementation-P3 and PRE-SVC-ML schedules match and stay unchanged. AM/AI annotations add no construction.\",\"mechanism\":\"Detach frees M; placement plus L routing supplies4. Unroute before lifting M, then restore H.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled: routing completes3; unrouting8, lifting9 and restoration10. Neither setup component alone suffices.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J07\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\",\"AM\",\"AI\"]}],\"handoff_residue\":\"Clip is conventional and cheaper in operator actions. Matching S/V and M/L across concerns predates assistance and cannot count as two new discoveries. Reassembly costs actions but is optional. Two synthetic source bodies, shared authorship, later mixed draws and unequal forwarded provenance do not prove independence, novelty or efficacy; first-study status remains unchanged.\",\"job_id\":\"COV-AC20-UNION-route0\",\"raw_sha256\":\"bdeb958e5f5c9895961172df885ad6151e7b04b208ac7578a3131e063f021759\",\"source_limits\":[\"Literal packet observations and finite-model predictions only; received replay verdicts are not observed physics.\",\"No source-derived physical property, unlisted operation, ladder change or hidden failure.\",\"Shared seed, distinct route and equal-union comparisons differ; no empirical independence, global originality or strategy efficacy established.\",\"Later coverage preserves valid original implementation and new service precursor without repairing original invalid service or regrading the gated first study.\"]},{\"candidates\":[{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"C\",\"op\":\"install\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"C\",\"op\":\"remove\",\"tick\":7}],\"burden\":\"Two actions, zero impacts; C occupied boundaries 3-8; H remains intact.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Late installation or early removal violates holding; unremoved C violates recovery.\",\"id\":\"UNION-C\",\"lineage\":\"Unchanged received PRE-SVC-C; AI informs endpoint accounting only.\",\"mechanism\":\"C alone supplies 4; removal frees C and permits separation.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled: install completes at 3, holding 4 through ticks 3-6; removal completes at 8. Four fewer actions than SV/ML. Conventional under J10.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J05\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\",\"AI\"]},{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"detach\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"V\",\"op\":\"install\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"S,V\",\"op\":\"insert\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"S,V\",\"op\":\"withdraw\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"V\",\"op\":\"remove\",\"tick\":8},{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"assemble\",\"tick\":9}],\"burden\":\"Six actions, zero impacts; S occupied until 8; V until 9; H unavailable while detached; optional restoration consumes one action.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Intact H blocks S use; insertion after tick 2 misses holding; withdrawal without V removal leaves a retainer.\",\"id\":\"UNION-SV\",\"lineage\":\"Unchanged overlapping implementation-P2/PRE-SVC-SV; AM/AI contribute relation checks, no new schedule.\",\"mechanism\":\"Detach frees S; installed V plus inserted S supplies min(4,4). Withdrawal then V removal clears the assembly.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled: holding begins at 3, ends at 8, V clears at 9, H restores at 10. Compared with pins, two fewer impacts and two more actions.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J06\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\",\"AM\",\"AI\"]},{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"detach\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"M\",\"op\":\"place\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"L\",\"op\":\"route\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"L\",\"op\":\"unroute\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"M\",\"op\":\"lift\",\"tick\":8},{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"assemble\",\"tick\":9}],\"burden\":\"Six actions, zero impacts; M occupied until 9, L until 8; S free; H unavailable until optional reassembly completes.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Placement alone cannot hold; late routing misses tick 3; omitting unroute or lift leaves release incomplete.\",\"id\":\"UNION-ML\",\"lineage\":\"Unchanged overlapping implementation-P3/PRE-SVC-ML; AM/AI contribute checks, not mechanism invention.\",\"mechanism\":\"Detach frees M; placement followed by L routing supplies min(4,4). Unroute then lift clears both components.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled: holding starts at 3, ends at 8, M clears at 9, H restores at 10. Same actions/capacity as SV, different occupied component and release primitives.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J07\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\",\"AM\",\"AI\"]}],\"handoff_residue\":\"Non-pin compound setups have no spare setup tick; withdrawal/unrouting ends holding before all component recovery. Reassembly is optional burden. Clip is conventional and lighter. Original implementation and later service coverage have different chronology. Equal-union information, shared seed and distinct routes are separate comparisons; none establishes independent efficacy or retrospectively repairs first-study verdicts.\",\"job_id\":\"COV-AC20-UNION-route1\",\"raw_sha256\":\"fda719f789b89cdf65d55a0c13184edbda0fb337227610a0591dcab997dff0d8\",\"source_limits\":[\"Only supplied packet and literal allowed source IDs; original source files were not read.\",\"Predictions are stipulated-model deductions; supplied replays are received evidence, not physical execution or self-grading.\",\"No field reliability, wear, global novelty, empirical independence, globally optimal schedule or method efficacy follows.\",\"Source-union differences and shared synthetic authorship limit causal claims; mixed chronology cannot regrade the gated original study.\"]}],\"source_routes\":[{\"forwarded_source_provenance\":{\"AC20-PRE-implementation\":{\"scope\":\"Literal received role data or selected summary only; original source bytes are not thereby supplied.\",\"source_ids\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J04\",\"J06\",\"J07\",\"J08\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J11\",\"J12\"]},\"COV-AC20-PRE-service\":{\"scope\":\"Literal received role data or selected summary only; original source bytes are not thereby supplied.\",\"source_ids\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J05\",\"J06\",\"J07\",\"J08\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J11\",\"J12\"]}},\"job_id\":\"COV-AC20-UNION-route0\",\"payload_sha256\":\"f00ec0c22571eaa1d9a065979ed272f5d21d0b1ab3c0dcfa1a15704857938691\",\"source_banks\":[{\"body_sha256_canonical_encoded\":\"8125e1fe9a4f7a2e812283fd737566e37cea5abd842cf346b95dcad6482c7759\",\"original_file_sha256\":\"5055c0b93d9a7c569f007ae97ad03033274e0e19645a74f0eb6a6a14a98494ec\",\"original_path\":\"/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/runs/2026-10-10-composed-ten/inputs/cases.json\",\"original_selector\":\"CONF\",\"selector_key\":\"route_information\",\"source_id\":\"AI\"},{\"body_sha256_canonical_encoded\":\"b3cdd1beca1904d3ae4a30f08c0c3439cc26a2d1c1dd28b42831c659821c7c40\",\"original_file_sha256\":\"5055c0b93d9a7c569f007ae97ad03033274e0e19645a74f0eb6a6a14a98494ec\",\"original_path\":\"/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/runs/2026-10-10-composed-ten/inputs/cases.json\",\"original_selector\":\"DEV\",\"selector_key\":\"route_material\",\"source_id\":\"AM\"}],\"source_exposure_manifest\":{\"distinct_empirical_datasets\":false,\"literal_bytes\":20471,\"selectors\":[\"route_material\",\"route_information\"],\"unique_bodies\":2}},{\"forwarded_source_provenance\":{\"AC20-PRE-implementation\":{\"scope\":\"Literal received role data or selected summary only; original source bytes are not thereby supplied.\",\"source_ids\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J04\",\"J06\",\"J07\",\"J08\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J11\",\"J12\"]},\"COV-AC20-PRE-service\":{\"scope\":\"Literal received role data or selected summary only; original source bytes are not thereby supplied.\",\"source_ids\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J05\",\"J06\",\"J07\",\"J08\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J11\",\"J12\"]}},\"job_id\":\"COV-AC20-UNION-route1\",\"payload_sha256\":\"a2fd69e551645ebeaa07faffcb432f80c5df765f95ba56b29c10041978e3a24c\",\"source_banks\":[{\"body_sha256_canonical_encoded\":\"8125e1fe9a4f7a2e812283fd737566e37cea5abd842cf346b95dcad6482c7759\",\"original_file_sha256\":\"5055c0b93d9a7c569f007ae97ad03033274e0e19645a74f0eb6a6a14a98494ec\",\"original_path\":\"/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/runs/2026-10-10-composed-ten/inputs/cases.json\",\"original_selector\":\"CONF\",\"selector_key\":\"route_information\",\"source_id\":\"AI\"},{\"body_sha256_canonical_encoded\":\"b3cdd1beca1904d3ae4a30f08c0c3439cc26a2d1c1dd28b42831c659821c7c40\",\"original_file_sha256\":\"5055c0b93d9a7c569f007ae97ad03033274e0e19645a74f0eb6a6a14a98494ec\",\"original_path\":\"/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/runs/2026-10-10-composed-ten/inputs/cases.json\",\"original_selector\":\"DEV\",\"selector_key\":\"route_material\",\"source_id\":\"AM\"}],\"source_exposure_manifest\":{\"distinct_empirical_datasets\":false,\"literal_bytes\":20471,\"selectors\":[\"route_material\",\"route_information\"],\"unique_bodies\":2}}]},\"construction\":\"The frozen capsule is a literal historical preservation target, not a newly proposed answer. Preserve every capsule value, including all 12 candidate records, their exact schedules and lineages, pool residues and source limits, the J0 case hash, both route identities, payload/raw/source hashes, selectors and forwarded-provenance scopes. A later summary-only builder may construct at most one source-bound solution and must distinguish its action selection from this frozen history. Unchanged contract: two initially aligned panels retain at least 4 at ticks 3,4,5,6, then separate with every installed retainer removed by boundary 10; no damage, discard, substitution or outside resource. One operator performs one allowed action per integer tick, completing next boundary. H starts intact; M and S become free only through detach(H). No resource occupies two places; at most one non-pin assembly and no pins with it. b remains 2; no ladder change. Three retained existing alternatives, with no revised actions: PROVENANCE-C=[2:install(C),7:remove(C)]. C supplies 4 at boundary 3, remains through the required hold ticks, and clears at boundary 8; two actions, zero impacts, intact H, conventional J10 construction. PROVENANCE-SV=[0:detach(H),1:install(V),2:insert(S,V),7:withdraw(S,V),8:remove(V),9:assemble(H)]. Detachment frees S, installed V plus inserted S supplies min(4,4)=4 from boundary 3; withdrawal ends retention at 8, V removal completes at 9, optional H restoration at 10. Six actions, zero impacts, S occupied until 8 and H unavailable while detached. PROVENANCE-ML=[0:detach(H),1:place(M),2:route(L),7:unroute(L),8:lift(M),9:assemble(H)]. M with routed L supplies min(4,4)=4 from boundary 3; unroute ends retention at 8, lift frees M at 9, optional H restoration at 10. Six actions, zero impacts, M occupied until 9 and L until 8. V installation or M placement alone is not holding; withdrawal or unroute alone is not complete recovery. The preserved two-pin family is AC20-PRE-implementation-P1=[0:tap(P1),1:tap(P2),7:pull(P1),8:pull(P2)]; intact H is required, two capacities of 2 add to 4, four actions and two impacts, conventional under J10. It remains in the capsule despite the exchange candidate cap. Restoration of H in the compound schedules is optional displaced work, not a hard panel-retention requirement and not extra capacity. The fresh builder can use the known clip schedule where appropriate without an originality claim. Do not infer unlisted adhesive, welding, sustained support or elastic behavior. Q cannot warrant 4 unmeasured; no measurement or oracle result is supplied to this role. Retain the exact J0 requirements and forward uncertainty rather than inventing a new mechanism.\",\"audit\":\"Actual joined-pool inspection: four pools each have three records, totaling 12. Semantic grouping by capacity-producing assembly, preconditions and action order yields four families: pins=1 record, clip=3, S/V=4, M/L=4. Route0 and route1 each retain clip, S/V and M/L with identical schedules. Wording variation is not mechanism diversity, and common precursor schedules are not independent discoveries. Supplied replay entries for all 12 report feasible, retention 4 at every required tick, no errors and no measurement; these are received finite-model results, not this role executing or self-grading current candidates. Source/candidate graph: J03+J04+J10 -> AC20-PRE-implementation-P1 -> preserved pins family. J05+J10 -> PRE-SVC-C -> COV-AC20-UNION-route0/UNION-C and COV-AC20-UNION-route1/UNION-C -> PROVENANCE-C. J03+J06 -> AC20-PRE-implementation-P2 and PRE-SVC-SV -> both routes/UNION-SV -> PROVENANCE-SV. J03+J07 -> AC20-PRE-implementation-P3 and PRE-SVC-ML -> both routes/UNION-ML -> PROVENANCE-ML. J01,J02,J09,J12 constrain every schedule. Received route graphs add AM dependency/resource-return annotations to S/V and M/L; AI adds state-versus-outcome/recovery accounting to all three retained families. Those source edges are interpretive checks, not sources of capacities, primitives or constructions. Source-lineage audit: the capsule preserves full initial lineages, each pool raw_sha256, candidate source_refs, limits and inconvenient residues. It also preserves both source-route payload hashes and route identities, AI original selector CONF/route_information and AM original selector DEV/route_material, canonical body hashes and the common original cases.json path/file hash. Both routes list the same two body hashes and exposure manifest: literal_bytes=20471, unique_bodies=2, distinct_empirical_datasets=false. Forwarded implementation provenance lacks J05 and forwarded service provenance lacks J04, so equal union at this later stage does not erase precursor exposure differences. Original source bytes are not supplied by these metadata. Received AM reports preparatory transfer versus correct release and returned rack space; received AI reports registration/request versus distinct recognition and stale displays. J0 has one operator and retention/removal, no two-clerk throughput, rack, FIFO queue or dashboard. Those received relations cannot import hidden J0 failures or physical laws. Qualified usefulness table, entirely modeled or received:\\nfamily | records | retention basis | operator actions/impacts | useful distinction | ceiling\\npins | 1 | two additive 2-unit pins with intact H | 4/2 | archived reference with H intact | conventional, no assistance addition\\nclip | 3 | C directly supplies 4 | 2/0 | least action burden among these retained schedules, intact H | conventional, no broader optimality claim\\nS/V | 4 | detached S inserted in installed V supplies min(4,4) | 6/0 including optional restoration | free M, occupy S; withdraw then remove V | existing precursor, no physical advantage established\\nM/L | 4 | detached placed M with routed L supplies min(4,4) | 6/0 including optional restoration | free S, occupy M; unroute then lift M | existing precursor, no physical advantage established\\nContrary dependencies and predictions: pin installation requires intact H; S/V and M/L require freeing a component by detachment. These are mutually incompatible resource-use choices, not inconsistent axioms. The possible inference that zero impacts require disassembly is defeated by the already supplied conventional clip. The actual compound proposals distinguish preparation from retention and retention termination from complete recovery; treating install(V), place(M), withdraw alone or unroute alone as full service would contradict their own stated dependencies. No such omitted release is invented as an actual defect in a supplied candidate. Actual remaining tension: S/V and M/L trade the same modeled retention and zero impacts for four extra actions versus clip and loss of H availability; they differ in which component is occupied. J0 supplies no subsequent demand for free M versus free S, and no wear or reliability model, so a compensating value or practical preference between these compound choices remains unsupported. Clip is already cheaper on the stated action dimension. No new mechanism opening is supported by this pool; the exchange contribution is a source-bound construction contract plus literal provenance transport. Q remains an uncertainty-bound refusal, not a guessed candidate. The audit identifies no hard axiom contradiction. Earlier incomplete handoffs and grades are neither supplied nor repaired. Python preserves the parsed frozen capsule as an unchanged object in the existing handoff.summary string; output creates no additional top-level provenance field.\",\"limits\":[\"This is separate later prospective provenance transmission coverage. Earlier incomplete handoffs and first grades remain unchanged; no earlier incomplete exchange or builder output was supplied or inspected.\",\"The 10000-word cap transports literal provenance and is not matched efficacy, equal information, equal compute or equal-search evidence. Six search slots, at most three exchange constructions, zero fresh builders here; a later builder remains capped at one construction.\",\"Only the literal assigned packet was read. Original source paths and hashes are forwarded identifiers, not proof this role opened or independently verified those files. AI and AM source-body observations are received route reports.\",\"Received replay results and current predictions concern stipulated J0 mechanics, not measured physics, native world execution, reliability, wear, global novelty, empirical independence or strategy efficacy. Root replays current action effects; this role does not award a final grade.\",\"No new capacity, operation, resource, simultaneous occupancy, pin/non-pin combination or impact ladder cell. Q_theta remains unknown in {0,4}; measurement creates no retention. No unconditional Q-only promise is advanced.\",\"Shared seed, distinct source routing and equal-union comparisons are different conditions. Matching source hashes, shared synthetic authorship and mixed original/later chronology cannot establish independent corroboration or retrospectively repair the gated first study.\",\"Known clip and two-pin constructions need no novelty claim. S/V and M/L predate both routed annotation and this exchange; preserving or renaming them adds no mechanism.\"]}",
    "residue": "Known clip is conventional and uses fewer actions than the compound schedules. Equal S/V and M/L capacity does not erase distinct component occupancy; optional H restoration adds burden. All inconvenient precursor/route residues survive inside the frozen capsule. No fresh source body or earlier incomplete exchange/builder was supplied. This later transmission result cannot repair first handoffs, regrade the first study or prove strategy efficacy."
